{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לא תנאף", :translit "lo tin'af", :gloss "you shall not commit adultery"} {:he "רצוח וגנוב ונאוף", :translit "retzoach v'ganov v'na'of", :gloss "murder, and steal, and commit adultery"} {:he "ש\"ז לבטלה", :translit "shin-zayin l'vatalah", :gloss "seed in vain"} {:he "ש\"ד", :translit "shin-dalet", :gloss "three [things]"} {:he "ולא תנאף", :translit "v'lo tin'af", :gloss "and you shall not commit adultery"} {:he "מאררים", :translit "m'or'rim", :gloss "those who curse"} {:he "ולא תגנוב", :translit "v'lo tignov", :gloss "and you shall not steal"} {:he "מים גנובים ימתקו", :translit "mayim g'nuvim yimatku", :gloss "stolen waters are sweet"} {:he "כיה עוד", :translit "k'hen od", :gloss "so they still"} {:he "נארבה לדם נצפנה לנקי חנם", :translit "n'eravah l'dam nitz'penah l'naki chinam", :gloss "let us lurk for blood, let us ambush the innocent without cause"} {:he "ולא תענה ברעך עדות שקר", :translit "v'lo ta'aneh v'rei'akha edut sheker", :gloss "and you shall not answer against your fellow false testimony"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 6, :occurrences ["מאררים"]} {:kind :other, :note "Superfluous vav in ולא תנאף corresponds to six occurrences of מאררים"} {:kind :other, :note "Superfluous vav in כיה עוד corresponds to six items listed in Proverbs 1:11"} {:kind :other, :note "Superfluous vav added to לא תענה — the world, created in six days, is afflicted"}], :frame {:text "The juxtaposition of the prohibitions teaches that one who emits seed in vain violates three commandments — murder, theft, and adultery — as stated in the Talmud: one who emits seed in vain is worthy of exile, and exile atones for three transgressions (Niddah 13b). The phrase 'stolen waters are sweet' is from Proverbs 9:17. The six things listed at the beginning of Proverbs are from Proverbs 1:11–14. The reading 'כיה עוד' with a vav reflects the masoretic spelling of Proverbs 9:17 (כן־עוד).", :sources ["Niddah 13b" "Proverbs 1:11-14" "Proverb